    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "THE GREAT WALL OF CHINA\nDONG KINGMAN",
      "Cocktails\nSherry Dubonnet Campari\nManhattan\nGin Martini Vodka Martini\nVermouth\nBloody Mary Screwdriver Whiskey Sour\nTom Collins Vodka Collins Daiquiri Scotch Bourbon\nCanadian Gin Vodka Rum Premium Beer\nMenus\nApéritif\nSelected Gourmet Delicacies\nt0****\nRoast au Vol\nA selected cut of aged beef, turkey or other succulent meat\nroasted on board and carved to order\nYour flight attendant will advise you of today's roast\nt 12\nChicken Normandy\nBoneless breast of chicken stuffed with apples and almonds\n***1-80,\nLobster Thermidor\nChunks of lobster in a creamy sauce laced with Madeira, Shery and Cognac\nLamb Curry\nTender lamb long simmered in an exotic and intriguing curry sauce\nPlat du Jour",
      "Chicken Normandy\nBoneless breast of chicken stuffed with apples and almonds\n** *1=*,\nLobster Thermidor\nChunks of lobster in a creamy sauce laced with Madeira, Shery and Cognac\nLamb Curry\nTender lamb long simmered in an exotic and intriguing cury sauce\nPlat du Jour\nAA*:\nPotatoes Maison\nButtered Vegetable Bouquet\n*\nTossed Garden Salad\nDessert\nSelection of Fruits and Cheeses\n******+\nTea\nGreen Tea\nCoffee\nDecaffeinated Coffee\nInternational Dateline Collation\nFresh California Fruit Salad\nEggs Mornay\nWith lime and honey dressing\nCrêpes à la Reine\nChicken crepes with grilled tomato\nCreamery Butter\nMushroom Omelette\nWith breakfast steak and grilled tomato\n6t0 t5\n7*++\nBreakfast Roll Basket\n$ 52\nHomemade Preserves\n* *\nMacademia Nut Wreath\nCoffee\nTea\n*I*\nGreen Tea Decaffeinated Coffee\n**\nSelected French Wines\nFrench Champagne Brut\nDrambuie Amaretto di Saronno Bénédictine\nCrème de Menthe Cognac VSOP\nContreau\n427 KC005(H)",
      "Dong Kingman, the award winning Chinese-American artist, travels the world sketching and painting\nthe beautiful, the monumental and the picturesque. His watercolors grace more than forty\npermanent museum and private collections in the USA and abroad\nIn the mountains north of Peking (Beijing), looking toward Inner Mongolia, is the Great Wall. The largest\nman-made structure on earth, the 3,000 mile wall was begun in the third century B.C. It took over\n200 years to complete. The Peking area also offers such wondrous sights as the Ming Tombs, the\nForbidden City, the Great Hall, Chairman Mao's Memorial and the Temple of Heaven. Shanghai,\nSoochow (Suzhou), Hangchow (Hangzhou), and Canton (Guangzhou), among many other cities,\nA visit to the People's Republic of China is a unique and totally remarkable experience: now, only\n14 hours away on Pan Am's 747SP Clippers\nOPAN AM\n0001, 080. 266"
    ],
